.TH CHECK-AI-IMAGES 1 "2026-11-08" "check-ai-images" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
check-ai-images \- scan subdirectories for AI-generation image metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B check-ai-images
[\fB\-v\fP]
[\fB\-d\fP]
[\fB\-n\fP \fIcount\fP]
[\fIdirectory\fP]
.br
.B check-ai-images
[\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B check-ai-images
inspects the image files inside the immediate subdirectories of the target
directory and reports which subdirectories contain images carrying
AI-generation metadata, using
.BR exiftool (1).
.P
For each immediate subdirectory (depth 1, not recursive), a sample of at most
.B 3
images is taken (jpg, jpeg, png, webp, avif, heic, heif, tiff, tif, bmp, gif,
jxl), keeping the first names in sort order. The sample size is settable with
.BR \-n ;
.B \-n 0
checks every image. All samples are then inspected with a single
.B exiftool \-j
run, split across a few parallel workers (one per CPU core, capped at 8).
Every metadata tag name and value is matched, case-insensitively, against the
detection patterns listed in DETECTION PATTERNS. A single match flags the whole
subdirectory.
.P
The summary header reports how many subdirectories and how many images were
checked, followed by:
.IP \(bu 2
directories containing AI metadata, prefixed
.B [AI]
.IP \(bu 2
directories with no AI metadata, prefixed
.B [--]
.IP \(bu 2
directories containing no supported image files, prefixed
.B [??]
(only shown if any)
.P
In verbose mode, the matching file and pattern are also reported to standard
error for each flagged directory, after the scan completes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose. For each flagged directory, print the triggering file and matched
pattern to standard error (the first pattern that matches, in the order of
DETECTION PATTERNS):
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
[AI]
\fIdirectory\fP
.TP
file:
\fIfilename\fP
.TP
match:
\fIpattern label\fP
.TP
tags:
\fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP ... (up to four matching tags, values cut at 200
characters)
.PD
.RE
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Debug. Implies
.BR \-v ,
but reports every matching sample in a directory rather than just the first,
and adds the offending metadata tags as
\fIkey\fP=\fIvalue\fP
pairs. Use this to confirm a detection (or spot a false positive) without
running
.BR exiftool (1)
by hand.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-number \fIcount\fP
Number of images to sample per subdirectory. Defaults to
.BR 3 .
.B 0
checks every image in the subdirectory, at roughly 2 ms per image. Ignored
when a subdirectory holds fewer images. The same value applies to every
subdirectory; there is no per-directory override.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print the usage summary and exit with status 1.
.TP
.I directory
Target directory to scan. Defaults to the current working directory. Must be
a directory; otherwise an error is printed and the script exits with status 1.
.SH DETECTION PATTERNS
An image is flagged if one of its metadata tag names or values matches one of
the following signatures:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Tool signatures
(substring match): Midjourney, Stable Diffusion, DALL\-E (also DALL\(pcE),
NovelAI, Leonardo AI, Adobe Firefly, Bing Image Creator, ComfyUI,
Automatic1111, InvokeAI, CivitAI, DreamStudio, craiyon, Artbreeder, Wombo,
DeepAI, NightCafe, Playground (Playground AI), Ideogram, Flux, SDXL, A1111,
DiffusionBee, Fooocus, RuDALL\-E, Kandinsky, SwarmUI, tidybot, StableSwarmUI,
Promptrr, PromptsPal, StylePrompt.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Generic AI labels:
AI\-generated, generated by AI, generated with AI, synthetic, AITag,
AIMetadata, AI_Generated.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Stable Diffusion PNG Parameters:
a
.I Parameters
tag whose value contains "negative prompt", "Negative prompt", "Steps:",
"Sampler:", "CFG scale", "Seed:", or "Model hash".
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan the current directory:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images
.EE
.P
Scan a specific tree:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images ~/Pictures
.EE
.P
Show which file and pattern triggered each detection:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images \-v ~/Downloads
.EE
.P
Show the exact metadata tags behind every detection (for verifying a hit):
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images \-d ~/Pictures
.EE
.P
Check every image in every subdirectory instead of three per directory:
.IP
.EX
check-ai-images \-d \-n 0 /mnt/data_storage
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed.
.TP
.B 1
Help was shown, an unknown option was given, the target is not a directory,
or a required tool is missing.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B exiftool
must be installed (from
.BR perl-image-exiftool ),
along with
.BR jq (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR exiftool (1),
.BR jq (1),
.BR find (1)
